  "term": "DTI",
  "definition": "DTI, or diffusion tensor imaging, is a diffusion-weighted MRI method that charts water movement in three dimensions. It is mainly used to visualize the brain’s white matter pathways and assess features of neural tracts such as their directional pattern and position, helping show subtle structural changes related to neuropathology or treatment.",
